(6578222, 979650, 112972, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gyaban:</b></div><hr/><i> Thanks Allen for the great information, especially regarding the stripbanks. They sure work beautifully. Also this shows that you also are a great studio photographer, I really admire your versatility. Congratulations on the ribbon!<br/> <br/>ETA: Is this a self portrait? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks!  Yeah, the strip-banks are great.  They give me a very narrow tunnel of light especially with the grids on.  For some odd reason, the grids are more expensive than the strip bank softboxes themselves.  I always leave the grids on.  Congrats on your blue!  Oui, c''est moi.</td>', 'Originally posted by gyaban: Thanks Allen for the great information, especially regarding the stripbanks. They sure work beautifully. Also this shows that you also are a great studio photographer, I really admire your versatility. Congratulations on the ribbon! ETA: Is this a self portrait?   Thanks!  Yeah, the strip-banks are great.  They give me a very narrow tunnel of light especially with the grids on.  For some odd reason, the grids are more expensive than the strip bank softboxes themselves.  I always leave the grids on.  Congrats on your blue!  Oui, c''est moi.', '2011-10-28 04:29:01.000000', NULL, 0),
